Creating unit tests for services and DAO (Data Access Object) in a Hotel Management project using Java
typically involves several steps. These tests will validate the correctness of your application's logic 
and ensure data is correctly being manipulated and stored/retrieved.

Let's break down the unit testing for both services and DAOs.

Tools and Libraries
1-JUnit: For writing and running the unit tests.
2-Mockito: For mocking dependencies such as DAOs or external service calls.
3-Spring Test (if using Spring Framework): For testing service layer, especially when dealing with databases.
4-H2 Database or In-memory database (optional for DAO testing): To avoid testing with real databases.

Example Scenario:
Let's assume you have a basic hotel management system with services like RoomService and DAOs like RoomDAO.

Example Class: RoomService

public class RoomService {
    private final RoomDAO roomDAO;

    public RoomService(RoomDAO roomDAO) {
        this.roomDAO = roomDAO;
    }

    public boolean bookRoom(int roomId) {
        Room room = roomDAO.findById(roomId);
        if (room != null && !room.isBooked()) {
            room.setBooked(true);
            roomDAO.update(room);
            return true;
        }
        return false;
    }

    public boolean cancelBooking(int roomId) {
        Room room = roomDAO.findById(roomId);
        if (room != null && room.isBooked()) {
            room.setBooked(false);
            roomDAO.update(room);
            return true;
        }
        return false;
    }

    public Room getRoomDetails(int roomId) {
        return roomDAO.findById(roomId);
    }
}

Example Class: RoomDAO

public class RoomDAO {
    private final EntityManager entityManager;

    public RoomDAO(EntityManager entityManager) {
        this.entityManager = entityManager;
    }

    public Room findById(int roomId) {
        return entityManager.find(Room.class, roomId);
    }

    public void update(Room room) {
        entityManager.merge(room);
    }

    public void delete(Room room) {
        entityManager.remove(room);
    }

    public List<Room> findAvailableRooms() {
        return entityManager.createQuery("SELECT r FROM Room r WHERE r.isBooked = false", Room.class).getResultList();
    }
}


Unit Test for RoomService (Using JUnit + Mockito)
import org.junit.jupiter.api.BeforeEach;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import org.mockito.InjectMocks;
import org.mockito.Mock;
import static org.mockito.Mockito.*;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

public class RoomServiceTest {

    @Mock
    private RoomDAO roomDAO;

    @InjectMocks
    private RoomService roomService;

    private Room room;

    @BeforeEach
    public void setUp() {
        room = new Room(1, "Deluxe", false);
    }

    @Test
    public void testBookRoomSuccess() {
        // Arrange
        when(roomDAO.findById(1)).thenReturn(room);

        // Act
        boolean result = roomService.bookRoom(1);

        // Assert
        assertTrue(result);
        verify(roomDAO, times(1)).update(room);
        assertTrue(room.isBooked());
    }

    @Test
    public void testBookRoomFailureRoomAlreadyBooked() {
        // Arrange
        room.setBooked(true);
        when(roomDAO.findById(1)).thenReturn(room);

        // Act
        boolean result = roomService.bookRoom(1);

        // Assert
        assertFalse(result);
        verify(roomDAO, never()).update(room);
    }

    @Test
    public void testCancelBookingSuccess() {
        // Arrange
        room.setBooked(true);
        when(roomDAO.findById(1)).thenReturn(room);

        // Act
        boolean result = roomService.cancelBooking(1);

        // Assert
        assertTrue(result);
        verify(roomDAO, times(1)).update(room);
        assertFalse(room.isBooked());
    }

    @Test
    public void testCancelBookingFailureRoomNotBooked() {
        // Arrange
        when(roomDAO.findById(1)).thenReturn(room);

        // Act
        boolean result = roomService.cancelBooking(1);

        // Assert
        assertFalse(result);
        verify(roomDAO, never()).update(room);
    }

    @Test
    public void testGetRoomDetails() {
        // Arrange
        when(roomDAO.findById(1)).thenReturn(room);

        // Act
        Room result = roomService.getRoomDetails(1);

        // Assert
        assertNotNull(result);
        assertEquals(1, result.getId());
    }
}


Unit Test for RoomDAO (Using JUnit + Mockito)
For testing RoomDAO, you'd typically mock your EntityManager and verify its interactions with the database.

import org.junit.jupiter.api.BeforeEach;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import org.mockito.*;
import javax.persistence.EntityManager;
import javax.persistence.Query;
import static org.mockito.Mockito.*;
import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;

public class RoomDAOTest {

    @Mock
    private EntityManager entityManager;

    @InjectMocks
    private RoomDAO roomDAO;

    private Room room;

    @BeforeEach
    public void setUp() {
        MockitoAnnotations.openMocks(this);
        room = new Room(1, "Deluxe", false);
    }

    @Test
    public void testFindById() {
        // Arrange
        when(entityManager.find(Room.class, 1)).thenReturn(room);

        // Act
        Room result = roomDAO.findById(1);

        // Assert
        assertNotNull(result);
        assertEquals(1, result.getId());
    }

    @Test
    public void testUpdateRoom() {
        // Arrange
        room.setBooked(true);
        doNothing().when(entityManager).merge(room);

        // Act
        roomDAO.update(room);

        // Assert
        verify(entityManager, times(1)).merge(room);
    }

    @Test
    public void testDeleteRoom() {
        // Arrange
        doNothing().when(entityManager).remove(room);

        // Act
        roomDAO.delete(room);

        // Assert
        verify(entityManager, times(1)).remove(room);
    }

    @Test
    public void testFindAvailableRooms() {
        // Arrange
        List<Room> rooms = List.of(room);
        Query query = mock(Query.class);
        when(entityManager.createQuery("SELECT r FROM Room r WHERE r.isBooked = false", Room.class)).thenReturn(query);
        when(query.getResultList()).thenReturn(rooms);

        // Act
        List<Room> availableRooms = roomDAO.findAvailableRooms();

        // Assert
        assertNotNull(availableRooms);
        assertFalse(availableRooms.isEmpty());
        assertEquals(1, availableRooms.size());
    }
}


Summary of Unit Tests:
1-Service Tests (RoomServiceTest):

Ensure methods like bookRoom, cancelBooking, and getRoomDetails work as expected.
Mock the DAO layer to focus on business logic.
Use assertions to verify correct behavior and interactions with DAOs.

2-DAO Tests (RoomDAOTest):

Mock the EntityManager and ensure that the database operations (e.g., findById, update, delete) are performed correctly.
Validate that correct queries are being run and results are returned.
